            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-5">33. Common Mistakes</h2>

            <ul>
                <li>Using tables for general page layout.</li>
                <li>Forgetting table headers.</li>
                <li>Incorrectly matching rows and cells.</li>
                <li>Using <code>rowspan</code> or <code>colspan</code> incorrectly.</li>
                <li>Creating very wide tables without responsive handling.</li>
                <li>Using too much inline styling.</li>
                <li>Creating unclear table structures.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-5">34. Best Practices</h2>

            <ul>
                <li>Use tables for actual tabular data.</li>
                <li>Use <code>&lt;th&gt;</code> for meaningful headers.</li>
                <li>Use <code>&lt;caption&gt;</code> when a table needs a title.</li>
                <li>Use <code>&lt;thead&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;tbody&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;tfoot&gt;</code> for larger tables.</li>
                <li>Use CSS for presentation and styling.</li>
                <li>Use responsive techniques for wide tables.</li>
                <li>Keep table structures simple and understandable.</li>
            </ul>

