            <div class="alert alert-info mt-4">
                <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">Summary</h2>

                <p class="mb-0">
                    HTML tables organize structured information into rows and columns.
                    The main elements are <code>&lt;table&gt;</code>,
                    <code>&lt;tr&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;th&gt;</code>, and
                    <code>&lt;td&gt;</code>. Larger tables can use
                    <code>&lt;caption&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;thead&gt;</code>,
                    <code>&lt;tbody&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;tfoot&gt;</code>.
                    The <code>colspan</code> and <code>rowspan</code> attributes
                    allow cells to span multiple columns or rows. CSS can be used
                    to create borders, spacing, alignment, hover effects, and
                    responsive table layouts.
                </p>
